B,F,G are collinear [09]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. CB = CA [00] & CE = CA [04] ⇒  C is the circumcenter of \Delta BAE [10]
002. C is the circumcenter of \Delta BAE [10] & A,B,C are collinear [01] ⇒  BE ⟂ AE [11]
003. BE = BC [05] & BC = BD [02] ⇒  B is the circumcenter of \Delta CED [12]
004. B is the circumcenter of \Delta CED [12] & B,C,D are collinear [03] ⇒  CE ⟂ DE [13]
005. E,D,G are collinear [08] & BE ⟂ AE [11] & CE ⟂ DE [13] ⇒  ∠GEC = ∠AEB [14]
006. A,B,C are collinear [01] & AB ⟂ BF [07] ⇒  CB ⟂ BF [15]
007. C is the circumcenter of \Delta BAE [10] & CB ⟂ BF [15] ⇒  ∠FBE = ∠BAE [16]
008. CE = CA [04] ⇒  ∠CAE = ∠AEC [17]
009. ∠FBE = ∠BAE [16] & ∠CAE = ∠AEC [17] & A,B,C are collinear [01] ⇒  ∠AEC = ∠FBE [18]
010. ∠GEC = ∠AEB [14] & ∠AEC = ∠FBE [18] ⇒  ∠GEA = ∠(EA-BF) [19]
011. E,D,G are collinear [08] & E,A,F are collinear [06] & B,F,G are collinear [09] & ∠GEA = ∠(EA-BF) [19] ⇒  ∠GEF = ∠EFG [20]
012. ∠GEF = ∠EFG [20] ⇒  GE = GF
